From e0512a9ac7fc6b69717bd8f7d96e465fe30308d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:17:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep restored retry waits pausable and fence legacy
 forwarding

Problem: repeated core update during a restored Retry-After wait could still
hold its reservation through the epoch; text-only owner forward lost custody.
Why1: pre-turn count0/empty history did not register watcher-visible work.
Why2: tracking expects a prospective reserved count, unlike boundary gating.
Root(happened): two consumers used different iteration-count contracts.
Root(not caught): prior repeat test requested pause BEFORE entering the wait.
Recurrence: extends original progressed 429 retry600 incident; no threshold waiver.

Use the prospective request count for tracking, retain original history for
persistence, and check the eligibility-only placeholder for the empty-history
continuation boundary. Legacy bare-text owner forward keeps its marker until
the absolute epoch; its existing retry remains per-turn, never a scheduler sleep.

Proof: new scheduler cold/cached, boot-sweep through real session.resume,
repeated pause after wait entry, owner-forward expiry and next-user controls.
Repeat RED dropped deadline at expiry; owner-forward RED forwarded early.
Unmodified b2b3badd process RED fails missing Retry-After custody after pause.
Fresh real-policy processes 3308135/3316457/3318440: unpooled 503 Retry-After600;
pause and repeat at production30s grace preserve1795216321.8712409; resumed
provider at1795216322.0743332, not early. Provider/UI doubles; no clock/policy
patches except restoring fixture constants to their production30s/1s values.
Not installed/live latency acceptance. Verifier retains five-natural-window
and original90s/180s targets, historical418/2284/2412s failures unchanged.
